    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.79"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Existing software and pattern catalogs support broad tests and directly establish examples such as Life. They cannot validate an exhaustive taxonomy over the unrestricted two-dimensional rule universe." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Sample defined families of two-dimensional rules, evolve random and sparse initial states, and classify one-dimensional time slices using preregistered order, entropy, periodicity, and localized-structure criteria. Test whether the resulting behaviors exhaust four categories and include robust class 4 examples." ;
